WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-DE

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.920
Hello.  Welcome back to Lam Rim.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.080
Today's session is a review of the entire course.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:18.000
That's good for me.  I would like to do a repeat performance for myself as well.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
In this format, where we produce individual episodes,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.840
one after the other, at different times,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.480
the flow of the entire instruction can be lost.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:33.240
Therefore, I think it's good if we start all over again

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.040
and then

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.160
repeat the entire previous Lam Rim instruction in one go.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.400
I use IDIMs for this, the idea pictures

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.800
we use to teach the ACI teachers.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.360
ACI teachers

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.120
are expected to be able to see one of the images

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.720
and identify the underlying concept.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:02.080
Tim, how many IDIMs do we have?  1,000 or so?  How many

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.120
?

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:10.720
500, something like that. So it's very easy to give an exam,

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.560
to test someone; we simply use the images.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.800
We'll just show you these pictures.  So,

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.120
in this repetition, I challenge you:

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.680
when we show a picture,

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.400
I give you one second and you see if you

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.000
can remember what the picture was about?

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.920
This is a good review of

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.120
this entire course.  Okay, let's begin.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.400
First picture, Mr. Sejii.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.680
This image is meant to remind you

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:48.880
that we are in the middle of the practices

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.800
for people with medium motivation,

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.600
and what they want is to reach Nirvana.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:00.640
They want to break free from the cycle of life, from all the suffering, for themselves alone.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.560
For this purpose, Buddha taught the three practices

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.520
that will help you reach your personal Nirvana.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.880
The third training is: understanding emptiness, understanding the pen.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.240
The second training is meditation.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:22.600
These two can only be truly deep in a quiet place,

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:28.720
at certain times of day, when you are really focused on your meditation mat.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.080
These two need to be taken really deep

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.880
at specific times of day.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.800
But the third one, the basis for the other two, being kind to others,

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.960
you can also call it morality,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.480
you can call it an ethical way of life,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.120
but in the end, it is being kind to others:

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.200
that is the basis

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.000
that is always available to us, all day long.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.240
This is one of the three extraordinary trainings of Buddhism,

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.160
and it is supposed to help us reach Nirvana.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.320
And it's available to us all day.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:06.960
In this picture

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.800
you can see Sejii helping Geshe Michael get to grips with his computer.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.560
Which is one of the kindest things young people can do for older people.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:22.760
Next picture.  See if you can remember what the picture means.  Do

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.440
you have any guesses?

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:35.480
This woman is doing her taxes.
Why is she doing this work in the Lam Rim system?

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.040
It makes her...

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:43.120
a Dharma master.  When I say Dharma Master or Tantra Master,

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:45.960
I can already see the image in your head:

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.920
a high lama, on a large throne with a large yellow hat.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:56.680
Perhaps he or she is holding a bell and a small drum and reciting mantras.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.080
And you think: "Oh, that's a Dharma Master. That's a real Dharma Master."

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.880
Or you could imagine the old image of Nagarjuna,

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.480
so mystical.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.640
But in Lam Rim we learned

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.640
that this woman, who

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:19.240
has children and is married,

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.680
is a Dharma Master.  She is a true Dharma master.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:29.120
Pabongka Rinpoche says: "Do not believe that a Dharma Master has to sit on a throne

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.520
and recite Tantra rituals."  What does

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:35.320
this woman do?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.080
She pays her taxes.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:44.480
Being honest about taxes is really difficult in my country.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.000
It can take you weeks to do your taxes properly, to

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:50.240


00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.600
make them completely honest, to

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.400
pay every single penny you are owed.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.840
That's what makes her...

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.040
she has the first of the extraordinary trainings of a good person,

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.040
being kind to others.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.720
That makes her a true Dharma master.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:11.080
So forget those pictures of llamas with big hats

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.960
ringing bells.  That's easy.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.680
Anyone can do it.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.040
Being kind to others is difficult.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.720
And upholding your morals, your ethics,

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.440
is also difficult.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.000
The next image:

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:32.120
I'll give you a moment.  Do
you remember what this is about?

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:40.680
The quote in the Lam Rim is:
TSUL KHRIMS LDAN PA'I DGE SLONG 'OD DANG LDAN

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.040
A person who truly keeps his vows,

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.240
truly keeps his Buddhist guidelines, especially the 10 guidelines,

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.000
he shines, he truly shines.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:06:00.160
A person who makes the healthy, modest, and reserved effort to keep their promises, to do

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:03.160
the 10 good karmas, and to be kind

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.400
to others,

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.080
has a kind of peaceful look on their face;

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.440
they radiate joy.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.840
When someone like that comes into the room, you know it.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:18.800
Everyone feels better, just like with Tim and Seijii.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:21.200
This is the light of the world.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.920
Buddha says these people are the light of the world.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.840
There is a Christian saying: Do

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:33.840
n't hide your light under a bushel, let the world see your happy face.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:41.320
And that is a true, guiding light for the entire world.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:45.080
The next picture, IDIM 4,

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:59.480
is a mountain cliff where I was with my partner Veronika on her birthday during this Lam Rim.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:08.320
The conversation was about the sunset,
in Tibetan NUB PA.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.080
This also means "west", because the sun sets in the west.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.960
NUB PA means

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.800
the sun is setting, and that is a very sad verb.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:22.440
That is a very sad thought in Dharma.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:29.000
The most famous passage is at the end of the Abhidharmakosha, "Treasury of Higher Wisdom".

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:33.440
"Treasury of Higher Knowledge" by Master Vasubhandu.  He says in it:

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:40.440
"The sun of Dharma, the light of Dharma, will set in the world."

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:44.920
We will lose the light of Dharma in this world.  This world will fall into darkness.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.000
After a certain period of time,

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:51.040
the teachings of the Buddha will disappear from this world.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:57.400
First they will disappear from people's minds, but they will still exist in libraries.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:01.280
These books will still be in the libraries.  Probably in libraries that John Brady hasn't found yet.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:05.680
And later they will have disappeared from the libraries as well.  And then they will be gone.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:13.600
I chose this image because Pabongka Rinpoche emphasized something special here.  He says:

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:21.000
"If you cannot keep your promises, if you cannot behave kindly towards others,

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.160
then we can say that the Dharma has left this world."

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:28.000
The light of Dharma has left this world within you.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:32.120
The sun has set in your own breast,

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.920
which would be a very sad thing if we do not keep our promises.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:38.520
Next picture.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:50.000
This retreat is called: "Love in the Time of the Virus".

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:56.920
The point is: In difficult times in the world,

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:59.080
if you keep your promises,

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:02.200
if you are kind to others,

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.760
in times when things are scary and eerie, when the virus is spreading,

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:08.080
nobody knows where, nobody knows how,

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.920
nobody knows how many people will die.  Doing

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:18.160
something kind for others during these difficult times

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.560
is all the more powerful.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:24.120
He mentions, if you remember, a 5-star Buddha paradise,

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:27.320
the perfect place:

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.440
It's easy to be a good person there,
everyone is a good person there.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.680
That's not a great achievement.  It's not a big deal

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.840
and the seed isn't that powerful:

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:40.080
being friendly in a group of friendly people.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:44.760
Being kind when people attack you, when they are afraid,

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:49.240
when others are not kind to each other, if you are that person

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:55.440
who stands up and shares things with others in difficult times,

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.280
then you are an extremely pure person.

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:02.480
That's great karma.  That's incredible karma, much more powerful.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.440
I think the virus is a very good time,

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.520
a very good opportunity for all of us to show

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:15.840
whether we are truly Buddhists,
whether we truly practice the Bodhisattva path.  Can

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:20.040
we help others, even when everything is extremely difficult?

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:22.960
Next picture.

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.680
This is difficult to remember; I have trouble with it myself.

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:37.720
I'll give you a second to figure out what this picture represents.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.640
Pabongka Rinpoche quoted from several works,

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:50.120
which, as different as they are, all have the same typical ending:

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:58.760
He quotes a famous ending: BLO BZANG RGYAL BA'I BSTAN PA ... CIG, which means:

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:04.040
May the teachings of the Victorious One,

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.120
Lobsang Drakpa, Je Tsongkapa,

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:09.480
spread throughout this world.

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:14.040
You think: We have to put this on the internet!

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.880
We need to translate this Lam Rim into many languages.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:23.480
We must try to bring these good words to as many people as possible.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:32.400
This is the end of the prayer, and now, after the end of this Lam Rim class or video, we should

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:36.800
share the Dharma with others.

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:39.720
We are meant to spread the Dharma throughout the world.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:45.240
In this part of the Lam Rim, Pabongka Rinpoche says:

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:52.160
"The place where you should spread the Dharma is here, in your own heart."  Do

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:57.000
n't think that "spreading Dharma" means translating the videos

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:02.120
into even more languages ​​or anything like that.
Yes, it is important to spread the Dharma in this way.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:06.920
But he says: If you spread it in your own heart,

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:11.480
then of course it will also spread outside of you, because the world comes from your heart,

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.800
or more precisely: from your heart chakra.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:18.600
Next picture, number 7.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:24.880
Try to remember what this picture was about.  I'll give you a few seconds.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:33.120
This is one of my favorite topics:

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:43.400
the personal relationship with another person, as these two people have it.  In

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:49.200
my opinion, and in Tantra, it is one of the most beautiful things that can happen to you.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.200
It's one of the greatest things you can experience.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:59.000
Anyone can tell you why the whole world is looking for a partner:

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.720
because it makes people happy.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:05.000
It is one of the greatest joys when things go well.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.000
It is one of the greatest joys you can experience,

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:14.120
but you and I also know:
when things don't go well,

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.800
it is one of the greatest sufferings in life.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:21.560
Why is this relevant to this course right now?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:30.520
If your ethics are good,

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.080
it is the greatest happiness in your life.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:38.000
And if you break your ethics, the same thing will make you unhappy.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:41.760
If you have a good woman or a good man as a partner,

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.120
then the same person who makes you totally happy can

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.640
also make you totally unhappy.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:54.040
So in this case, Vinaya, your personal practice of kindness,

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.680
of good behavior, is compared to a partner

00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:01.440
who brings out in you either the best you can be in this life

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:04.760
or the worst - the same person.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.600
Next IDIM, number 8.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.600
That was a complicated picture.  Do you remember?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.240
I take a sip of my green smoothie.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.160
Thank you, Vimala.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:35.040
This is about breaking your promises.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:40.680
Pulling up weeds represents breaking your promises.

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:46.680
Why does the destruction of this plant symbolize the breaking of your promises?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:53.040
If you are a gardener, you know that you must remove the weeds

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.120
before their seeds ripen.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.920
If you wait until the seeds are about to fall off

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:03.280
and only then remove the plant,

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:06.080
you will spread thousands of seeds.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:12.440
And a month, a year later, you will see a thousand times more weeds sprouting.

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.920
So you need to pull out these weeds early.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:20.560
This refers to a very radical statement

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:22.800
made by the Buddha:

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:29.240
DGE SLONG DAG SROG DANG BRAL ZHING SHI BA NI BLA'I

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.680
Better to die

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.960
than to break your promises.  How come?

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:37.000
If you break your promises,

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:40.360
you will sow seeds

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:44.160
that will multiply for many lifetimes.

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:51.080
If you die now, you have ruined a mind-body connection.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:55.440
If you die now, you will ruin a very useful temple,

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:58.800
a body temple, and a spirit temple.
You will lose ONE such connection.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.040
But if you break your promises,

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.920
you lose many mind-body connections.

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.920
You're ruining body and mind for many lifetimes.

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:12.920
You are planting seeds

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.720
that will ruin many lives.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:21.880
Buddha said: It is better to die than to break your promises.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:28.920
And he didn't mean that metaphorically.
He meant it quite literally

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:32.720
when he said: Better to die than to break your promises!  There's

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.800
this joke in Lam Rim.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:45.760
We take a vow never to give up Bodhichitta, not even if it costs us our lives.  There's

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:53.960
this famous saying:
Our whole lives we expect to be

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:56.040
put in prison

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.240
by some evil people.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:03.960
They threaten you with a knife and say: "Abandon your Bodhisattva vows, or you will die now!"

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.120
And we then reply:

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.960
"I choose death!"

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.600
And they are killing us.

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:14.720
I think we've all been waiting for a situation like this since we took that vow.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:19.720
We're waiting for these guys to show up with knives and threaten us.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:24.320
But actually, WE are the guys with the knives.  We threaten our Bodhisattva vows every day.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:33.200
Every day we have to make the decision whether or not to carefully keep our promises.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:39.200
It's difficult to find those types who will put you in prison and say,

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:42.920
"I will kill you if you don't renounce your Bodhisattva vows."

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:48.040
Next picture.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:56.040
See if you can remember.  I'll give you a moment, try to remember.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.200
That was a hint at...

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:10.440
In our "Mixed Nuts" translator team,

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:14.040
we translated an old Vinaya test:

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.920
The monks' and nuns' vows.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:26.560
It was about the vow, the tradition we are not supposed to break:

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:31.160
When you become a monk or nun, you get your robe,

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.200
a small Buddhist statue,

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.320
and a sieve.

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:40.720
In ancient India, you always had to have this sieve with you.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:44.800
To drink water from a river,

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:50.920
you should first filter the water to ensure that you don't kill any small insects.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:57.000
We have mentioned a famous tradition from the Vinaya:

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:00.680
When some monks go to the water,

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.840
to the river, to fetch water,

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:08.800
they should choose the friendliest monk to test the water.  Do

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:16.440
n't choose the guy who doesn't care about insects.  Take the one who loves insects,

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:20.720
let him test the water, for he will be more attentive.  What is this about

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:23.400
?

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.920
We talked about "ecological vows,"

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:33.040
where monks and nuns are not even allowed to tear the leaves off a plant

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:39.040
because they are home to tiny creatures.

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:44.400
It means that you must respect even the smallest vows;

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:50.600
take them very seriously, because the results will increase exponentially.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:55.080
Furthermore, it is important to maintain your ethics at a very subtle level,

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:59.840
at a very refined level.  And please: Don't overdo it!

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:04.040
If I were to write the Bodhisattva vows,

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:06.040
I would include an extra Bodhisattva vow about

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:08.600
not overdoing it with your Bodhisattva vows.

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:11.200
There's nothing more annoying

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:15.880
than a person informing you that they are keeping their vows

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.080
and therefore have to be an asshole today.

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.600
Keep your vows in a loving way. Joyfully.  Don't overdo it.  Do

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:31.080
n't bother other people with your vows.  The vows are not meant to bother other people with them.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:36.720
Keep the small vows, keep them quietly, personally, don't make a demonstration out of them.

00:20:37.760 --> 00:20:43.560
There is an expression in Islam: Don't let the right hand know what the left hand is doing.

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:48.120
It means that you should not ostentatiously display your vows.  Keep them still and quiet.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:51.200
And at a very high level.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.040
Next picture.  The point

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:06.120
here is that being kind to others

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:10.240
is like planting a tree.

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:13.400
Today I went to the PeachTree Cafe to

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:16.080
check something.

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:20.440
Stanley, Allison and I planted a peach tree there

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:25.080
when we first did the PeachTree Cafe Morning Show.

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:29.760
I want to tell you that 3 peaches grew on it this week;

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:32.800
we now have peaches.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:40.160
This means: Pay attention to your basic practice.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:44.560
Pay attention to the root.  Plant kind karma

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:47.920
by keeping your vows, by being kind to others.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:49.960
A tree will grow from it.

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:52.440
And the peach tree that we

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:55.080
planted about 5 months ago is

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:58.040
already bearing lots of fruit.

00:21:58.600 --> 00:22:05.040
If you hadn't taken care of him when he was little, you wouldn't have anything now.

00:22:05.040 --> 00:22:08.200
If you take care of the foundation of your Buddhist practice,

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:10.800
being kind to others,

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:14.120
then you will reap thousands of fruits.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:16.160
That's how it will be.  It will grow

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.160
into a huge tree

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:23.480
that produces peaches every year.
You will have peaches for years to come.

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:25.560
Hold and protect them.

00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:29.560
This child in the picture has carefully protected the seedling.

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:31.960
Protect your ethics.

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:34.520
Next picture.

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:41.320
If I remember correctly, there are 4 conditions

00:22:42.240 --> 00:22:45.080
that can lead to you breaking your obligations.

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:47.080
If you have taken the Bodhisattva vows,

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:50.440
or the Vinaya Pratimoksha vows,

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:53.840
or even the Diamond Way, the Tantra vows—

00:22:54.800 --> 00:23:00.200
I believe there were four—Pabongka Rinpoche summarized them... perhaps there were more...

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.920
anyway, there are specific conditions

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.080
that will help you break your vows.

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:09.240
If you want to break your vows, there are a few specific ways to do it.

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:10.320
Here's the first one:

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:16.440
If you don't know your vows,

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:21.000
that's a good indication that you'll break them.  If you want to break them,

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:22.720
then simply don't study them!

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:27.080
One of the things that bothers me, and there are many things that bother me about the Dharma,

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:33.800
is teachers who give initiations, major initiations,

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:38.600
but they don't explain to the people taking the initiations

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.520
that they have just taken vows.

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:44.840
When you undergo an initiation, there are hundreds of vows that you take at the same time,

00:23:45.760 --> 00:23:48.320
and you will break them if you don't know them.

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:51.120
It is the teacher's responsibility to teach

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:55.400
you the vows before you receive initiation.

00:23:56.320 --> 00:24:01.080
If he or she does not offer you such instruction, then I would not accept any initiation from him or her.

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:07.080
The best way to break your vow, the first way, is not to know it.

00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:09.400
Read the recipe before you start cooking.

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:12.720
Veronica tells me that every time I cook.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.160
Next picture.

00:24:17.000 --> 00:24:23.360
A woman who says: "It's not a big deal."

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:33.600
This vow, not to cut any leaves without prayer, come on,

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:40.400
that's really extreme.  That's a bit too much, not that important.

00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:43.000
It's just about a few insects

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:47.560
that might occasionally use this leaf as a roof.

00:24:47.560 --> 00:24:50.040
It's not a big deal.

00:24:50.480 --> 00:24:53.800
The second major way to break your vows

00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:55.400
is precisely this attitude:

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:59.200
"Oh, the vow isn't that important, I'd rather keep the important ones."

00:25:00.200 --> 00:25:02.120
The next picture.

00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:12.400
When we have a Klesha attack, when something negative

00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:16.920
dominates our mind, it's an excellent opportunity to break our vows:

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:20.600
becoming angry at someone

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:26.280
or something, wanting to have it desperately, e.g., money,

00:25:26.600 --> 00:25:29.480
or being addicted to Netflix every night.

00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:36.000
...By the way, there's nothing wrong with watching Netflix, but what I'm talking about is

00:25:38.960 --> 00:25:43.200
hurting someone because you desperately want to go home to watch Netflix.  That's the problem here.

00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:46.920
This picture is called Gang Fighting.

00:25:46.920 --> 00:25:50.400
What's the story behind it?

00:25:52.120 --> 00:25:56.040
Always go after the biggest guy in the opposing gang first.

00:25:57.000 --> 00:25:59.000
Find out who the leader of the other side is, do

00:25:59.560 --> 00:26:04.080
n't argue, don't negotiate, don't shout at each other,

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:07.000
go up to him and punch him.

00:26:07.480 --> 00:26:10.800
And then the entire opposing side will be defeated as well.

00:26:11.080 --> 00:26:15.080
Identify your biggest bad habit

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:19.000
and take care of it first.  This is one way to keep your promises.

00:26:21.200 --> 00:26:23.200
The next picture.

00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:30.640
Incidentally, at my age—

00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:33.760
I won't tell you how old I am—

00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:37.080
this whole "young love" thing

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:40.160
is so ridiculous from the perspective of my age.

00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:44.800
I can say that from experience, because I've experienced it myself.

00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:48.240
But this whole thing about:

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:50.800
Oh, she's the most beautiful woman in the world.

00:26:51.400 --> 00:26:53.400
He is the most attractive man in the world.

00:26:54.440 --> 00:27:01.120
My older brother once said something funny:

00:27:01.120 --> 00:27:02.920
"You like the girl?"  I said "Yes".

00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.480
He asked: "Do you want to spend your life with her?"
I said "Yes".

00:27:06.160 --> 00:27:08.160
Then he said: "Look at her mother first.

00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:16.120
Look at what her mother looks like."  I said, "Your mother looks terrible. She is overweight, she looks tired and terrible."

00:27:16.920 --> 00:27:21.800
And he said, "What do you think she looked like before?"

00:27:22.040 --> 00:27:24.240
Think about it.

00:27:25.480 --> 00:27:29.560
If you are so fixated on a person's appearance,

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:35.280
or something physical, something not really important about a person:

00:27:35.480 --> 00:27:40.200
that will change.  You will witness this person become ill and grow old.

00:27:40.200 --> 00:27:44.000
You will witness her having diarrhea and vomiting.

00:27:44.240 --> 00:27:48.040
If you're unlucky, you might see her intestines during an operation.  Do

00:27:49.080 --> 00:27:52.120
n't kid yourself, don't

00:27:53.080 --> 00:27:55.080
think it's worth hurting others to

00:27:55.760 --> 00:28:00.680
get the most beautiful woman or man ever.  It's not worth it.

00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:08.600
It won't stay that way.  It's wonderful to be in a relationship, but you should be in it for the right reasons.

00:28:09.200 --> 00:28:11.200
The next picture.

00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:15.080
If you have a problem with anger,

00:28:16.160 --> 00:28:18.160
or you get easily upset,

00:28:18.320 --> 00:28:21.080
then develop this fantasy of giving this person

00:28:21.760 --> 00:28:24.480
something they would like to have.

00:28:24.480 --> 00:28:27.480
That's called maître, jampa

00:28:27.480 --> 00:28:28.120
love.

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:33.400
Develop this imagination, remember how wonderful it is to give someone something

00:28:34.040 --> 00:28:36.160
they like or want.

00:28:36.200 --> 00:28:38.240
Develop this attitude.

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:42.040
If you are not well-disposed towards another person,

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:45.880
then fantasize a little, meditate on

00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:50.440
how you can give that person something they truly desire.

00:28:51.000 --> 00:28:53.000
The next picture.

00:28:54.040 --> 00:29:00.040
I'll give you a moment, I bet you can't remember!

00:29:01.480 --> 00:29:03.400
Tim cheats and flips ahead.

00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:10.040
What was this about?  For

00:29:11.080 --> 00:29:13.960
pride.

00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:17.840
Pride is also an obstacle to keeping your promises.

00:29:18.720 --> 00:29:22.120
One of the most typical forms of pride

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:29.680
in the monastery, where this work was mainly taught,

00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:35.280
is the amount of your knowledge about the scriptures, how many facts you have already gathered

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:37.120
in your life.

00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:41.280
I, for example, love to collect obscure Dharma facts,

00:29:41.280 --> 00:29:43.080
and the more you acquire,

00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:47.080
the more special you feel.

00:29:48.040 --> 00:29:52.960
Pabogka Rinpoche says: "All the Dharma you have ever learned in your life, all the things you have memorized,

00:29:52.960 --> 00:29:54.720
all the things you have debated,

00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:56.800
all the Geshe degrees you can earn:

00:29:58.480 --> 00:30:04.160
compared to what there is still to learn, you know nothing.

00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:07.560
You are like a worm on the ocean floor that

00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:12.000
sometimes swims to the surface and looks at the stars.

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:15.680
Many of these stars are surrounded by planets.

00:30:16.520 --> 00:30:20.440
There are people on these planets. There are
things to know about these people.

00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:24.480
The things we know,

00:30:24.720 --> 00:30:27.200
this knowledge we are so proud of,

00:30:27.680 --> 00:30:33.880
all of this is just a tiny fraction of what you could know.

00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:37.200
So don't be proud.

00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:39.200
The next image.

00:30:43.000 --> 00:30:47.240
One of the great motivations for breaking your promises,

00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:54.240
your vows, your ethics, the thing that will keep you from reaching Nirvana, the thing that will keep you from

00:30:55.080 --> 00:30:57.680
reaching the second stage of Lam Rim: your personal Nirvana,

00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:03.000
is not understanding emptiness! Therefore,  Study emptiness.

00:31:04.320 --> 00:31:06.320
When you realize that the mean things

00:31:06.920 --> 00:31:08.920
someone does to you

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:13.240
come directly from what you did last week,

00:31:13.960 --> 00:31:18.240
you won't make big mistakes.
The more you study emptiness, the

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:22.440
more you study cause and effect, dependent origination—

00:31:23.000 --> 00:31:25.280
which means: This person comes from my seed!—the

00:31:26.360 --> 00:31:33.760
easier it will be to keep your promises. The easier it will be, so study, study, study.

00:31:35.560 --> 00:31:41.320
I had a teacher, an old teacher from Mongolia, he was very old and had tuberculosis, and

00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:48.720
he said:

00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:56.240
"He is really good."  You're so proud, you have this huge mountain of pride, from Princeton and

00:31:57.080 --> 00:31:58.720
later from this Geshe thing,

00:31:58.720 --> 00:32:00.800
which is very helpful, very helpful...

00:32:00.880 --> 00:32:03.960
you'll try harder,

00:32:04.440 --> 00:32:06.440
just to look smart.

00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:11.600
That's quite lucky, but later on, stop doing that.  "

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:15.080
Just learn to be a good person." That was very funny.

00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:19.000
He gave me Adam's text on his deathbed.

00:32:19.760 --> 00:32:21.760
I remember.

00:32:24.040 --> 00:32:25.960
The next picture.

00:32:25.960 --> 00:32:30.320
This is technically the 4th cause, right? No.

00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:37.040
One of the reasons you break or lose your vows is:

00:32:37.560 --> 00:32:39.680
It's very difficult in the modern world to

00:32:40.120 --> 00:32:45.960
keep your mind on your vows when you have a lot to do, when everything has to be done quickly. There

00:32:46.520 --> 00:32:48.920
are a thousand things to look at on the internet,

00:32:49.680 --> 00:32:53.000
and life is moving so fast.

00:32:53.440 --> 00:32:58.640
It's hard to maintain that self-awareness: Am

00:32:58.640 --> 00:33:03.080
I breaking my vows right now, am I doing something that will hurt someone else?

00:33:03.840 --> 00:33:08.680
You need to slow down a little, come back to your vows,

00:33:09.080 --> 00:33:14.720
and maintain a kind of vigilance and sensitivity to

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:19.880
the fact that you made promises not to hurt others.

00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:24.160
The busier the situation becomes, the more mindful you need to be.

00:33:25.680 --> 00:33:31.000
It's very easy to get annoyed with your partner when you're very busy.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:33.200
He or she wants to tell you something,

00:33:33.960 --> 00:33:36.320
and you have to do 10 things at once.  You're working through your tasks and you exclaim,

00:33:37.840 --> 00:33:42.120
"I don't have time to listen to you right now.

00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:45.960
My boss has given me ten things to do."

00:33:46.440 --> 00:33:48.440
These are exactly the times when you need to slow down,

00:33:49.200 --> 00:33:51.200
when you need to remember your vows. Above

00:33:51.280 --> 00:33:55.000
all, don't forget your promise to be kind to others,

00:33:55.680 --> 00:33:59.200
even when you're very stressed and very busy.

00:33:59.960 --> 00:34:04.440
It's better to break business promises

00:34:05.760 --> 00:34:10.040
than to be nervous, stressed, and unkind to others.

00:34:11.200 --> 00:34:14.040
It's better to not pay a bill, or miss a business meeting,

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:17.560
or not be quite as good at work as you could be

00:34:18.720 --> 00:34:23.560
if that means keeping your mind clear.

00:34:25.080 --> 00:34:27.080
The next picture.

00:34:27.480 --> 00:34:30.840
A woman buying a useless thing at a store.

00:34:33.200 --> 00:34:35.200
Try to remember the story.

00:34:36.800 --> 00:34:42.160
She says, "Oh, this box is so beautiful." She goes to the department store and buys it.

00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:44.600
...what's the name of that store

00:34:45.080 --> 00:34:48.480
where you can buy things like that? Crate and Barrel.

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:54.040
She goes to Crate and Barrel in the USA. She says, "Oh, my husband will love this box."

00:34:54.520 --> 00:34:57.480
She has no idea what for.  She will use them,

00:34:58.040 --> 00:35:00.040
but she takes them home with her.

00:35:04.320 --> 00:35:09.400
Then she comes home and her husband says, "Are you crazy?"  This is a completely useless box.

00:35:09.400 --> 00:35:16.280
We have enough trash in our house.  Bring them back.  "Get your money back."

00:35:16.920 --> 00:35:23.800
Should she drive to the gas station and try to return the box there?

00:35:24.120 --> 00:35:31.000
No, because that's not where she bought it. This is obvious, but we still have to say it.

00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:33.480
If you buy a stupid box

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:38.240
because you like it and you think your husband will like it, but he doesn't...

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:41.920
And if he asks you to return the box, do

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:46.160
n't take it to another store. Take it back to where you bought it.

00:35:46.720 --> 00:35:53.160
What does that mean?

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:58.080
You should pay me!

00:35:59.680 --> 00:36:01.680
When it's time for a confession,

00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:03.480
if you've broken a vow,

00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:06.960
try to do it with the person who gave you the vow.

00:36:07.080 --> 00:36:12.120
Confess in the presence of the person who gave you the vow.

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:17.320
Is it okay to confess to myself at home?

00:36:17.680 --> 00:36:22.280
Not for vows you took from other people!

00:36:22.720 --> 00:36:27.200
Generally speaking, if you didn't take a vow from someone else,

00:36:27.200 --> 00:36:29.160
it might be okay

00:36:29.280 --> 00:36:34.080
to confess at home, in front of a Buddha statue or something like that.  In extreme cases, that's okay.

00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:36.120
But generally speaking,

00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:39.800
if you can go to the person who gave you your vows

00:36:40.160 --> 00:36:45.200
and confess openly to them—then forget the shame. We're shameless all day long.

00:36:45.840 --> 00:36:49.080
Forget the shame about your vows and tell yourself, "What the hell?"

00:36:49.960 --> 00:36:52.720
Go straight to your teacher and say, "I broke this pesky vow."

00:36:53.200 --> 00:36:57.160
And your teacher is like, "Wow, you're a really bad person." And you're like, "Yeah, that's right!"

00:36:57.400 --> 00:37:03.000
Get it over with, and then you'll feel so pure, you'll feel so good.

00:37:03.520 --> 00:37:07.320
You can be shy about many things in life, but don't be shy about your vows.

00:37:07.320 --> 00:37:11.000
If you break a vow, tell someone,

00:37:11.000 --> 00:37:14.240
and that's how you get rid of it. You get rid of the problem.

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:20.000
If you keep it to yourself and if you spend more time hiding it

00:37:20.040 --> 00:37:23.200
instead of confessing or keeping it, then that's just stupid,

00:37:23.480 --> 00:37:26.600
and it won't make you feel any better. You won't  Feel it purely.

00:37:27.480 --> 00:37:33.160
Just be open with your teachers: I have this problem. I have this bad habit.

00:37:33.560 --> 00:37:38.040
Then the karma is destroyed, the seed is destroyed.

00:37:38.320 --> 00:37:47.880
Your teacher will say, "I've heard that before, you've told me that before." But persist and tell him or her again.

00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:50.320
Next picture.

00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:57.680
This is about... remember?

00:38:01.160 --> 00:38:04.440
It's about honoring

00:38:04.800 --> 00:38:08.080
the small details of the vows again.

00:38:08.400 --> 00:38:13.680
This, by the way, is a vow for monks to
brush their teeth

00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:16.320
with a stick called a so-shing.

00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:18.440
That's a stick you're supposed to use to brush your teeth.

00:38:18.600 --> 00:38:21.280
You just cut it from a tree and use it.

00:38:22.160 --> 00:38:24.160
That's a toothbrush.

00:38:24.320 --> 00:38:31.440
And the vow says monks should have toothbrushes and brush their teeth.

00:38:31.840 --> 00:38:34.040
It might seem like a small thing:

00:38:34.920 --> 00:38:38.920
"Wait, I'm trying to keep my tantric vow here to get into Amitabha's paradise

00:38:39.560 --> 00:38:43.080
and protect all living beings!" And Buddha says, "Yes, but in the meantime,

00:38:43.080 --> 00:38:46.240
could you please..."  Brush your teeth every day.

00:38:46.240 --> 00:38:49.560
And you think to yourself: That's not exactly a grand vow.

00:38:50.040 --> 00:38:53.800
Yes, but it is precisely the little things that make up the Buddha's paradise.

00:38:53.800 --> 00:38:57.680
It is the small things that Bodhisattvas do,

00:38:58.040 --> 00:39:00.120
those who are kind to others.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:03.840
Of course, everyone in the world will

00:39:05.080 --> 00:39:09.840
end a nuclear war if they can.  I mean, that's obvious.

00:39:10.160 --> 00:39:12.960
But are you kind enough as a person

00:39:13.200 --> 00:39:16.400
that you wouldn't even want to subject others to your bad breath

00:39:16.800 --> 00:39:18.360
if it might offend them?

00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:20.720
If you are very sensitive

00:39:21.080 --> 00:39:24.600
about the little things that could hurt other people,

00:39:24.920 --> 00:39:27.200
then we can say that you maintain your ethics.

00:39:28.160 --> 00:39:33.680
And then it's the small details that complete the final brushstrokes

00:39:34.240 --> 00:39:40.600
on your Buddha paradise, which you can see in the next picture.

00:39:41.480 --> 00:39:47.280
This person is decorating a Christmas tree...

00:39:47.800 --> 00:39:52.240
I don't know if you've ever decorated a Christmas tree, but those of us who were raised in the Christian tradition were given

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:55.000
the task of decorating the Christmas tree by our parents.

00:39:55.840 --> 00:39:58.560
And it's something special to

00:39:58.920 --> 00:40:01.800
hang the last ball.

00:40:01.800 --> 00:40:06.920
Everyone looks at the Christmas tree and asks, "Is it finished?"  and then it's: "Yes, he's finished!".

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:11.480
But then they say: "Wait, we should hang another one right here!"

00:40:12.040 --> 00:40:15.680
This Christmas ornament

00:40:16.040 --> 00:40:22.000
is your teeth brushing.  It's the small final details

00:40:22.240 --> 00:40:28.720
that you add to your Buddhahood.  It is the little things that the Buddhas create.

00:40:28.720 --> 00:40:32.160
It's not the great things.  It's not the big things.  It is attention

00:40:33.080 --> 00:40:35.000
to the small details

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:41.240
that make other people happy that creates a Buddha.

00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:45.240
The next picture.

00:40:45.560 --> 00:40:55.080
Try to remember this.  Here's a tip for you: Yamantaka!

00:40:57.000 --> 00:41:01.520
This is a famous Lam Rim story.

00:41:01.960 --> 00:41:06.040
Monks and nuns are to go to the Sojong twice a month and confess to each other, openly,

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:09.240
what mistakes we have made

00:41:09.400 --> 00:41:12.440
.

00:41:13.080 --> 00:41:15.080
The teacher says:

00:41:15.200 --> 00:41:18.320
They hit the GUNTY,

00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:22.600
a special piece of wood, it looks like a square timber,

00:41:23.200 --> 00:41:27.600
and you hit it with another wooden stick and it goes tong, tong, tong...

00:41:28.160 --> 00:41:33.400
and that is then a bell, an old bell, before bells were made of metal.

00:41:33.400 --> 00:41:38.080
The timber was being felled, and when you heard it,

00:41:38.240 --> 00:41:41.360
you had to go to the Sojong.
They still do that today.

00:41:41.680 --> 00:41:44.920
I built a gunty with my teacher.  He wanted one

00:41:45.200 --> 00:41:47.560
and we built it in the right size;

00:41:47.960 --> 00:41:49.600
you have to follow all sorts of rules.

00:41:49.880 --> 00:41:51.880
If you hear that gunty,

00:41:52.240 --> 00:41:54.240
it will be held that way.

00:41:54.600 --> 00:41:57.360
You hold the gunty here and hit it like this.

00:41:58.040 --> 00:42:01.960
And then all monks and nuns are expected to make their profession of faith.

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:06.240
So this teacher says: "You have beaten the gunty. Let's go."

00:42:06.520 --> 00:42:09.200
And the student says, "No, I'm not going to confess today."

00:42:10.160 --> 00:42:12.160
The teacher asks: "What?"

00:42:12.440 --> 00:42:17.200
For that is one of the main obligations of a monk, to go to the Sojong.

00:42:17.960 --> 00:42:20.600
The teacher says: "What are you talking about?"
And the student says, "I don't have to go today."

00:42:21.400 --> 00:42:24.080
The teacher says, "What do you mean, you don't have to go today?"

00:42:24.120 --> 00:42:27.920
He says, "Have you already forgotten, you gave me the Yamantaka initiation yesterday?

00:42:28.320 --> 00:42:33.080
I am Yamantaka, I am Buddha. I don't need to go to the Sojong anymore."

00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:38.160
The teacher pulls his ear and says, "Yes, of course, you are Yamanika!

00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:44.120
Yamantika will come with me to the Sojong, right now."

00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:48.440
This means: Don't tell me what a great Tantrika you are,

00:42:49.080 --> 00:42:51.640
and that you are above ethics

00:42:51.640 --> 00:42:54.080
and now have a higher vision -

00:42:54.800 --> 00:42:58.440
that is a completely false concept!

00:42:58.920 --> 00:43:02.040
If you have received a secret initiation,

00:43:02.600 --> 00:43:05.600
then you should go to the Sojong every morning.

00:43:05.840 --> 00:43:08.400
You should go even more often than others.

00:43:08.400 --> 00:43:10.760
Because that is exactly what will

00:43:11.000 --> 00:43:14.920
give you the energy for your tantric practice:
being kind to others

00:43:14.920 --> 00:43:16.720
and admitting when you have made a mistake.

00:43:17.480 --> 00:43:21.800
The next picture.

00:43:22.520 --> 00:43:29.080
That's a sad picture.
We always imagine ethics as the root of

00:43:29.080 --> 00:43:32.800
our practice, the basis of our practice.

00:43:33.120 --> 00:43:35.960
Pabongka Rinpoche sees it exactly the opposite way:

00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:38.800
That is the perfect picture.

00:43:38.800 --> 00:43:42.240
He says: Imagine an apple tree that

00:43:42.440 --> 00:43:46.160
someone has cut in half.  In his example, it was a palm tree.

00:43:47.400 --> 00:43:52.360
Someone had cut it in half and removed the crown.

00:43:52.720 --> 00:43:55.080
You will have no leaves,

00:43:55.360 --> 00:43:58.040
not a single leaf will grow.

00:43:58.320 --> 00:44:00.440
That means you won't have any flowers either.

00:44:01.480 --> 00:44:05.080
And that's why you won't get any fruit from the blossoms.

00:44:05.840 --> 00:44:07.880
You won't get anything at all.

00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:14.480
A person who is not kind to others, day after day, hour after hour,

00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:19.680
eliminates any possibility of

00:44:20.160 --> 00:44:23.560
reaping these beautiful fruits of their practice.

00:44:23.680 --> 00:44:28.880
The next picture.

00:44:32.160 --> 00:44:34.920
This is about something my teacher asked me...

00:44:36.800 --> 00:44:42.440
Sorry, something I asked my teacher, and I don't know if you remember, but I asked him: You reach

00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:50.520
the first of the five paths, the path of accumulation,

00:44:50.800 --> 00:44:55.440
when you experience a personal tragedy,

00:44:55.840 --> 00:44:59.080
but if you are on the Bodhisattva path,

00:44:59.400 --> 00:45:01.560
you reach it when you attain Bodhichitta.

00:45:01.560 --> 00:45:06.560
And I asked him: I don't understand what is supposed to be tragic about Bodhichitta?

00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:09.000
And he said, "No, no.

00:45:09.280 --> 00:45:12.440
The subject is still a tragedy.

00:45:13.000 --> 00:45:19.200
But it is the tragedy of every living being. Every being in the entire universe

00:45:20.120 --> 00:45:23.000
experiences the same tragedy."

00:45:23.440 --> 00:45:30.000
This shared tragedy is the true beginning of the 5 Paths.

00:45:30.160 --> 00:45:32.200
Reflecting on this tragedy

00:45:32.520 --> 00:45:35.600
is the beginning of the 5 paths for a Bodhisattva.

00:45:35.600 --> 00:45:37.120
So, in reality, it's the same thing.

00:45:37.560 --> 00:45:43.560
The puppy is having a hard time, but now all the puppies in the basket are having a hard time.

00:45:44.040 --> 00:45:46.040
We're all in this together.

00:45:46.040 --> 00:45:49.600
And that is the beginning of Bodhichitta.

00:45:50.160 --> 00:45:53.560
Next picture.

